Identity Team, IT Ops, Application Owners,

REMINDER - SAML SIGNING CERTIFICATE
EXPIRING JULY 21.

The IdentiCore IdP signing certificate
for your tenant
(acme.identicore.example) expires
July 21. Update the certificate in
your SPs (or federation proxy)
before then, or SSO logins will
fail across your SAML apps.

1. ROTATION DETAILS

  Tenant:        acme.identicore.example
                 (IdP)
  Current cert:  expires 2027-07-21
  Affected:      14 SAML SPs (VPN
                 portal, wiki, BI
                 suite, HR system)
  Cadence:       every 2 years
                 (last: July 2025)

2. HOW TO ROTATE (OFFICIAL PATH
   ONLY)

    1. Download the new metadata
       from YOUR TENANT'S
       well-known URL:
       https://acme.identicore
       .example/saml/metadata
       - type it yourself. This
       URL is the only valid
       source of your IdP
       metadata.
    2. Verify the new
       certificate's
       fingerprint in your
       admin console (the
       console displays the
       upcoming cert under
       Certificate Lifecycle).
    3. Import into SPs /
       federation proxy;
       rollover metadata
       (old + new cert) keeps
       sessions alive during
       the switch.

  IdentiCore will NEVER:
  - Email metadata packages
    as attachments for SAML
    rotations (a SAML
    metadata file sent by
    email and imported
    wholesale is the classic
    certificate-injection
    attack: whoever's key
    is in the imported
    metadata can forge
    assertions for every
    app that trusts it -
    full authentication
    takeover. Metadata
    comes from the tenant's
    well-known URL, TLS-
    protected, or not at
    all)
  - Provide a "bulk import"
    lane pushing one package
    to many SPs via an
    emailed page
  - Use lookalike domains
    such as
    "identicore-ops" or
    "ic-metadata"

3. THE FINGERPRINT RULE

  The malicious variant of
  this notice tells you to
  "verify the fingerprint"
  of the attached file -
  against a value printed
  in the same email. That
  proves nothing: both the
  file and the number come
  from the attacker. The
  only meaningful
  comparison is attachment
  (or any downloaded file)
  versus YOUR admin
  console or YOUR tenant's
  HTTPS URL - fetched
  independently of the
  email.

4. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

  - Cert expiry and the
    upcoming certificate
    appear in your admin
    console (typed address)
    under Certificate
    Lifecycle
  - The 2025 rotation
    followed the same
    URL-only flow
  - Report lookalike
    rotation notices to
    security@identicore.example
    immediately -
    metadata phish are the
    highest-severity class

